.page id 1 print user and group identities

# SYNOPSIS
*id* [*-ugGnr*] [_USER_]

# DESCRIPTION
`id` prints the user id and the group ids of the current user, or of _USER_, as names and numbers: `uid=1000(reimu) gid=1000(reimu) groups=1000(reimu),100(shrine)`. Group membership comes from the fourth field of `/Hakurei/etc/group`.

# OPTIONS
@ *-u*
    Print only the user id.
@ *-g*
    Print only the primary group id.
@ *-G*
    Print all group ids, separated by spaces.
@ *-n*
    Print names instead of numbers (with `-u`, `-g` or `-G`).
@ *-r*
    Accepted and ignored.

# EXAMPLES
    id
    id -un
    id marisa

# SEE ALSO
whoami(1), groups(1), passwd(5), group(5)
